 <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 italic">USB PD 3.1 doubles max power from 100W to <strong>240W via EPR</strong> (28V/36V/48V), a single USB-C cable now charges everything from earbuds to gaming laptops. The EU mandate requires USB-C for all notebooks from <strong>April 2026</strong>, making PD 3.1 mandatory for laptop charger OEMs. For B2B buyers: GaN PD 3.1 chargers start at <strong>MOQ 500, FOB Shenzhen $8-22/unit</strong>. Above 100W, you need both an EPR-rated charger AND EPR e-marker cable, one without the other caps you at 100W.</p>
