 </div>
 <div class="bg-brandBlue/10 border-l-4 border-brandBlue p-5 rounded-r-xl">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-2">The Bottleneck Rule</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Your charging speed is limited by the <strong>weakest link</strong> in the chain: charger → cable → device. A 240W PD 3.1 charger with a basic 3A cable delivers only 60W. A 100W charger with an EPR cable still delivers only 100W. All three components must support the target power level. This is the #1 reason people don't get the charging speed they paid for. For full guidance, see our <a href="/blog/usb-c-pd-fast-charging-guide/" class="text-brandBlue hover:underline">USB-C PD Fast Charging Guide</a>.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
